use std.spec
use std.spec.step
use os.services.vfs.vfs.{VfsManager, Filesystem, SeekWhence}
use os.kernel.types.fs_types.{FileFlags, FsNode, FsNodeKind, DirEntry}
use os.apps.file_manager.file_manager.{SortField, SortDirection, FileEntry, FileManager, format_size, format_kind, kind_icon}
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001 — behavior under test holds under execution.
"""
## Purpose and audience

Executable specification for the FileManager application: construction
defaults, sort comparison and ordering, navigation, selection bounds,
the show-hidden toggle, set_sort, the format helpers, and the open-path
resolution helpers. Audience: os.apps.file_manager owners and reviewers
confirming file-manager behavior still holds before a change lands.

## Operator workflow

1. Run `bin/simple test test/01_unit/os/apps/file_manager/file_manager_spec.spl`.
2. Every scenario must pass; a failure is a regression in file-manager behavior.

## Compatibility and limitations

Known defect (2026-09-05): the FileManagerOpenStatFs mock does not
implement the `stat_no_follow` and `readlink` methods the Filesystem
trait requires, and the module does not provide the imported kind_icon,
so the file fails at LOAD and executes zero scenarios; the spec is kept
byte-for-byte RED until the trait gain methods are implemented on the
mock. Platform-specific behavior is out of scope.

## Verification guidance and troubleshooting

Re-run the single file to reproduce; today the failure is the trait
conformance error above, not any assertion. Once the mock implements
stat_no_follow and readlink, a failing scenario names the file-manager
operation and the expected value.
"""
